<title>CHINA: China's Beijing ITIC mandates US$77 mln loan.</title>
<headline>China's Beijing ITIC mandates US$77 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beijing International Trust and Investment Corp (BITIC) has mandated Societe Generale Asia to arrange a US$77 million term loan, bankers said.</p>
<p>The loan has a maturity of five years.</p>
<p>Pricing details were not available.</p>
<p>There is a letter of comfort from Beijing Municipal Planning Commission.</p>
<p>BITIC is the state-owned finance institution and investment vehicle of the Beijing Municipal Government.</p>
<p>- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6960</p>
